  "implementation": [
    "Service resolves only live metadata in its own bounded Core registry. Caller Conversation/Session and optional UUID must agree. Unknown/expired/mismatched URLs remain unresolved; no selector triggers arbitrary network IO or falls back to a supplied UUID.",
    "Native PeerCommand admission carries the resolved resource DTO under original current peer/source guards; signed original envelope and exact Core fetch custody remain unchanged. HTTP derives current source policy under its original bearer fence. No Store or protocol/schema change.",
    "The public fetch backend resolves the original locator again and checks the full actual Store scope, including Tenant. Fresh current source policy and exact record binding govern projection; a conditional hash names this newly authorized view.",
    "Only explicit fetch backend instances receive the registry. Runtime/trusted persistence backend keeps local lookup behavior. Direct HTTPS GET still requires its original viewer, revision, hashes and reference lifetime; control selection cannot reactivate an expired link."
  ],
  "behavior": [
    "Both supported signing algorithms use actual native and HTTP public SDK fetches with URL+hash, matching optional UUID and byte-for-byte matching authorized metadata. Large vCon bodies follow fresh pinned authenticated references.",
